{"schema_version":"1.0","safety_id":"SFTY-20211210-26603","identifiers":[{"type":"safety","value":"SFTY-20211210-26603"},{"type":"ghsa","value":"GHSA-jfh8-c2jp-5v3q"},{"type":"cve","value":"CVE-2021-44228"}],"affected_packages":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"maven","registry":["Maven Central"],"name":"org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-core","purl":null,"description":null},"description":null,"is_transitive":false,"is_transitive_cross_ecosystem":false,"vulnerable_specs":[">= 2.13.0, < 2.15.0",">= 2.4, < 2.12.2",">= 2.0-beta9, < 2.3.1"],"spec_standard":null,"first_patched_versions":["2.15.0","2.12.2","2.3.1"],"recommended_version":"2.15.0","reachability":null}],"description":{"summary":"Remote Code Execution (RCE) in Log4j","advisory":"Remote Code Execution (RCE) in Log4j","original_advisory":"Remote code injection in Log4j","short_description":"Remote Code Execution (RCE) in Log4j","long_description":"Affected versions of this package are vulnerable to Deserialization of Untrusted Data leading to Remote Code Execution (RCE). JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker controlled LDAP and other JNDI related endpoints. An attacker who can control log messages or log message parameters can execute arbitrary code loaded from LDAP servers when message lookup substitution is enabled. \n\nThe Apache Logging Services team provided updated mitigation advice upon the release of version 2.16.0, which disables JNDI by default and completely removes support for message lookups.\nEven in version 2.15.0, lookups used in layouts to provide specific pieces of context information will still recursively resolve, possibly triggering JNDI lookups. This problem is being tracked as [CVE-2021-45046](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-45046). \n\n### Workaround\nUsers who want to avoid attacker-controlled JNDI lookups but cannot upgrade to 2.16.0 must ensure that no such lookups resolve to attacker-provided data and ensure that the JndiLookup class is not loaded.\n\n### References\n[https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jfh8-c2jp-5v3q](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jfh8-c2jp-5v3q)"},"references":[{"name":"URL","url":"https://getsafety.com/vulnerabilities/SFTY-20211210-26603/CVE-2021-44228"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-44228"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://github.com/apache/logging-log4j2/pull/608"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://github.com/tangxiaofeng7/apache-log4j-poc"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/changes-report.html#a2.15.0"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/lookups.html#JndiLookup"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3198"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3201"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/manual/migration.html"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://logging.apache.org/log4j/2.x/security.html"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://packetstormsecurity.com/files/165225/Apache-Log4j2-2.14.1-Remote-Code-Execution.html"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/12/10/1"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/12/10/2"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/12/10/3"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://psirt.global.sonicwall.com/vuln-detail/SNWLID-2021-0032"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3214"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/alert-cve-2021-44228.html"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/12/13/1"},{"name":"URL","url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2021/12/13/2"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/LOG4J2-3221"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-7rjr-3q55-vv33"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/pdf/ssa-661247.pdf"},{"name":"URL","url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-l